$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=evalsttlem  LOC_AFTER=?

* Sufficient condition for evaluating in time: for F : A --> Option A and N <= M, the state X evaluates within M steps to the N-th iterate of the option-lifted step at some X. This is how a test program is certified: exhibit the step count and compute the iterate.

1::simp1l   |- ( ( ( A e. V /\ F : A --> ( A |_| 1o ) ) /\ ( M e. NN0 /\ N e. ( 0 ... M ) ) /\ X e. A ) -> A e. V )
2::simp1r   |- ( ( ( A e. V /\ F : A --> ( A |_| 1o ) ) /\ ( M e. NN0 /\ N e. ( 0 ... M ) ) /\ X e. A ) -> F : A --> ( A |_| 1o ) )
